==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|fr|lang=en}} {{term|cor||lang=fr|horn}} + {{term|anglais||lang=fr|English}}, calqued from a misunderstanding of {{etyl|gmh|fr}} ''engellisches Horn'' ("angelic horn"), from the resemblance of the instrument to horns played by angels as depicted in the Middle Ages.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cor anglais|head=[[cor#French|cor]] [[anglais#French|anglais]]}}

# A double reed [[woodwind]] [[instrument]] in the [[oboe]] family that is pitched in F, a fifth lower than the oboe and is consequently approximately one-third longer than the oboe.

====Synonyms====
* [[English horn]]

